However, I do run into scenarios where my functions end of getting nested within one another, both relying on mirai calls, but they are already within it. Currently it spins up another daemon within that mirai to keep going. It would be desirable to a) detect if you are in a mirai call already so you can make an educated decision and b) optionally let the nested mirai call use the existing deamons. Not sure how possible that is, I couldnt tell from #89. 

